[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Members Low Level Requirements
UID: GSSC-MEMBERS-LOW-LEVEL-REQUIREMENTS
VERSION: 5.0.0

[GRAMMAR]
ELEMENTS:
- TAG: TEXT
  FIELDS:
  - TITLE: UID
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: STATEMENT
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
- TAG: SECTION
  PROPERTIES:
    IS_COMPOSITE: True
    PREFIX: None
    VIEW_STYLE: Narrative
  FIELDS:
  - TITLE: UID
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: TITLE
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
- TAG: REQUIREMENT
  PROPERTIES:
    PREFIX: GSSC-MLLR-
    VIEW_STYLE: Table
  FIELDS:
  - TITLE: UID
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: TITLE
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: STATEMENT
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: RATIONALE
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: COMMENT
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: DERIVED
    TYPE: SingleChoice(True, False)
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: VERIFICATION_METHOD
    TYPE: SingleChoice(Test, Inspection)
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: CHANGE_DRIVER
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: REVIEW_STATUS
    TYPE: SingleChoice(Changed, Approved, Baselined)
    REQUIRED: True
  RELATIONS:
  - TYPE: Parent
    ROLE: Refines
    REVERSE_ROLE: Refined By

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-INTRODUCTION
TITLE: Introduction

[TEXT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-INTRO-FRAMEWORK
STATEMENT: >>>
GSSC5-80 scaffolds this Members LLR document and the members Vitest harness. It claims no GSSC-MLLR-* requirement UIDs (mirrors public GSSC5-39: no testing-framework LLRs).
<<<

[TEXT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-INTRO-UID-BLOCKS
STATEMENT: >>>
UID allocation for this document (coordinate parallel tickets before minting):
GSSC5-79 Member FE Root + Router owns GSSC-MLLR-1 through GSSC-MLLR-13.
GSSC5-81 Member Header owns GSSC-MLLR-14 through GSSC-MLLR-31.
GSSC5-82 Member Footer owns GSSC-MLLR-40 through GSSC-MLLR-66 (Footer chrome, contact details, Key-Value Store, and Society Contact).
GSSC5-87 Logout / Session Service owns GSSC-MLLR-67 through GSSC-MLLR-71.
GSSC5-86 Login Page owns GSSC-MLLR-72 through GSSC-MLLR-91.
GSSC5-88 Route Guards & Redirects owns GSSC-MLLR-92 through GSSC-MLLR-95.
GSSC5-83 Member Generic Sections (display) owns GSSC-MLLR-96 through GSSC-MLLR-124.
GSSC5-100 Hide Header/Footer when logged out owns GSSC-MLLR-32 (App Root chrome gate; also CHANGE_DRIVER on GSSC-MLLR-1).
GSSC5-90 Account Self-Service and GSSC5-91 Admin Account Management share GSSC-MLLR-125 through GSSC-MLLR-158 (same Account Page).
GSSC5-85 Contact-row / Form Primitives owns GSSC-MLLR-159 through GSSC-MLLR-179 (Contact Row + form-field building blocks).
GSSC5-84 Generic Editor Module owns GSSC-MLLR-180 through GSSC-MLLR-201 (editor shell, actions, contention, session behaviors; composes GSSC5-85 form fields).
GSSC5-92 Members Directory + Search owns GSSC-MLLR-202 through GSSC-MLLR-214 (exact end 214; band 202–230 reserved for directory so parallel Wave tickets do not mint below 231).
Parallel Wave tickets (GSSC5-89, 93–97) start at GSSC-MLLR-231 and above.
GSSC-MLLR-33 through GSSC-MLLR-39 remain free for later claimants.
Do not reuse numbers already claimed by another ticket.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-APP-ROOT
TITLE: Member App Root

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-APP-ROOT-ELEMENT
TITLE: App Root

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-1
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend App Root SHALL contain a Page Outlet. When the member is logged in, the App Root SHALL also contain a Header host and a Footer host.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The App Root composes those subelements so Header, the active Member Frontend view, and Footer share one shell for authenticated contents. Header and Footer contents are separate requirements. Logged-out states omit Header and Footer hosts so the login experience is not wrapped in authenticated chrome.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-79
GSSC5-100
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-13
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-2
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend App Root SHALL fill the entire viewport.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The App Root is the outermost shell of the Member Frontend page. Filling the viewport gives Header, page content, and Footer a full-page layout that resizes with the viewport.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-79
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-13
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-3
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend App Root SHALL use the white theme token for its background and the sans-serif theme font for its text.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The outermost Member Frontend layer uses a white background and a sans-serif default. Theme tokens supply those values.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-79
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-13
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-HEADER-HOST
TITLE: Header Host

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-4
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Header host SHALL hold the Member Frontend Header.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The App Root supplies a host so Header implementation mounts in the Member Frontend shell. Header contents are separate requirements.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-79
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-13
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-15
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-5
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Header host SHALL stick to the top of the viewport while the member scrolls.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Authenticated Member Frontend views keep the Header at the top. Sticking the host keeps that top placement as the member scrolls.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-79
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-15
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-6
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
The Header host SHALL inherit the App Root font and text color theme tokens.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The Header host is an empty mount for Header contents. It inherits App Root type tokens so the shell stays consistent until Header paints its own presentation. Independent Header host colors are not set yet.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-79
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-15
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

