[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-ROUTER
TITLE: Member Router

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-13
TITLE: Home Page Route
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend Router SHALL open the Member Frontend home page at the root path.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The Member Frontend home page for a logged-in member is the dashboard destination. This route places that home page at the root path so navigation and redirects share one entry.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-79
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-26
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-HEADER
TITLE: Member Header

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-HEADER-BAR
TITLE: Header

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-14
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend Header SHALL present the Header Logo, and when a member is logged in SHALL present the Header Navigation, the Header Greeting, and the Header Logout control, and when no member is logged in SHALL present the Header Login control.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The Header composes those displayed elements in the Header host. Each element's behavior is a separate requirement. This is Member Frontend chrome with login and logout affordances, not a Public Frontend Header action-bar clone.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-81
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-15
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-15
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend Header SHALL fill the Header host and arrange identity, navigation, and account-access controls in a horizontal bar that wraps as the viewport narrows.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The Header host already sticks to the top of the viewport. Filling that host and wrapping the bar keeps Header contents available as the page resizes.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-81
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-15
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-16
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend Header SHALL use the light-green theme token for its background, the gray theme token for a thicker bottom border, and the dark-green theme token for its text.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Theme tokens keep Header presentation aligned with the organization palette shared with the Public Frontend Header. A fuller color role map for the Member Header is not set yet beyond these token choices.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-81
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-15
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-HEADER-LOGO
TITLE: Header Logo

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-17
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Header Logo SHALL display the GSSC Logo, and selection of the Header Logo SHALL open the Member Frontend dashboard.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The Header always includes the GSSC Logo so the member can identify the society. Selecting the logo returns the member to the Member Frontend dashboard home.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-81
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-16
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-18
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Header Logo SHALL appear at the start of the Header in every layout.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Leading placement keeps the logo visible as the primary identity mark in the Member Header.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-81
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-16
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-19
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
The Header Logo SHALL use the dark-green theme token for its mark color.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A single theme token keeps the mark readable on the Header background until a brand color role is set.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-81
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-16
  ROLE: Refines

