[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-HEADER-NAV
TITLE: Header Navigation

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-20
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
When a member is logged in, the Header Navigation SHALL provide a control that opens the Member Frontend dashboard and a control for each other Member Frontend area that member is permitted to open.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Logged-in members reach the dashboard and permitted Member Frontend areas from the Header. Area inventory grows as those areas land; this requirement covers the navigation affordance, not Public Frontend Contact or Site Search controls.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-81
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-19
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-21
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Header Navigation SHALL appear after the Header Logo when a member is logged in, and SHALL be omitted when no member is logged in.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Navigation sits with identity for logged-in members. Omitting it when logged out keeps the Header focused on login until authentication succeeds.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-81
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-19
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-22
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
The Header Navigation SHALL use the sans-serif theme font and the dark-green theme token for its text color.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Navigation shares Header text tokens until a fuller control style map exists.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-81
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-19
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-HEADER-GREETING
TITLE: Header Greeting

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-23
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
When a member is logged in with a valid Member Frontend session, the Header Greeting SHALL display a greeting that includes that member's name.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The greeting shows a logged-in member that the Header recognizes the session and identifies the member by name.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-81
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-17
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-24
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Header Greeting SHALL appear among the Header account-access controls when a member is logged in, and SHALL be omitted when no member is logged in.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The Greeting is the logged-in account-access signal. Omitting it when logged out leaves room for the Header Login control.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-81
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-17
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-25
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
The Header Greeting SHALL use the sans-serif theme font and the dark-green theme token for its text color.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The Greeting shares Header account-access text tokens so it reads with Login and Logout.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-81
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-17
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-HEADER-LOGOUT
TITLE: Header Logout

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-26
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
When a member is logged in, the Header Logout control SHALL end that member's Login Token session and leave the visitor logged out.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Logout ends the Unified Backend Login Token session for that member and clears Member Frontend logged-in presentation. Full route-guard redirects after logout are separate requirements.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-81
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-18
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-9
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-27
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Header Logout control SHALL appear among the Header account-access controls when a member is logged in, and SHALL be omitted when no member is logged in.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Logout sits with the Greeting for logged-in members and is hidden when there is no session to end.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-81
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-18
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-28
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
The Header Logout control SHALL use the sans-serif theme font and the dark-green theme token for its text color.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Account-access controls share Header text tokens until a fuller control style map exists.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-81
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-18
  ROLE: Refines

