[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-LOGIN-BEHAVIOR
TITLE: Login Form Behavior

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-90
TITLE: Enter Submits Login
STATEMENT: >>>
When the visitor presses Enter while focus is in the Login Identity Field or the Login Password Field, the Login Page SHALL submit login the same way as activating the Login Submit control.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Enter-to-submit matches other Member Frontend forms and speeds credential entry.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-86
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-4
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-91
TITLE: Login Field Validation
STATEMENT: >>>
When login is submitted with an empty Login Identity Field or an empty Login Password Field, the Login Page SHALL mark each empty field invalid and omit Unified Backend login until both fields have values.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Client-side required validation matches other Member Frontend forms and avoids useless backend round trips.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-86
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
