[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-GUARDS
TITLE: Route Guards and Redirects

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-92
TITLE: Unauthenticated Redirect With Return Path
STATEMENT: >>>
When a logged-out visitor requests Member Frontend contents other than the login experience, the Member Frontend SHALL redirect that visitor to the login experience and include the attempted Member Frontend path in the login query.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Protected contents stay gated behind login. Carrying the attempted path lets a later successful login return the member to that destination.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-88
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-10
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-93
TITLE: Explicit Logout Login Landing
STATEMENT: >>>
When a logged-in member chooses Header Logout and the session ends, the Member Frontend SHALL take that visitor to the login experience without a return-path query for the page they left.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Explicit logout is a deliberate session end. Landing on login without a return path avoids sending the member straight back into the view they just left.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-88
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-9
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-94
TITLE: Authenticated Login Redirect
STATEMENT: >>>
When a logged-in member requests the login experience, the Member Frontend SHALL redirect that member away from login to the return path in the login query when that path is a safe Member Frontend destination, otherwise to the Member Frontend home path.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
An already-authenticated member does not need the login form. Honoring a safe return path keeps deep-link behavior consistent; home is the fallback.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-88
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-12
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-95
TITLE: Post-Login Destination
STATEMENT: >>>
When login succeeds, the Member Frontend SHALL take the member to the return path from the login query when that path is a safe Member Frontend destination, otherwise to the Member Frontend home path.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Returning to the requested destination avoids an unnecessary detour through home after an unauthenticated deep link. Home remains the fallback.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-88
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-11
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[/SECTION]]

