[[/SECTION]]

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-SECTION-FROM-CUID
TITLE: Section From CUID

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-120
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend Section From CUID SHALL retrieve a section's data from the Unified Backend using the section cuid it receives, building Section Contents from that data: the header when that data includes a header, the body, resources when that data includes resources, using each backend resource string as that resource's name and that resource's target, and the optional image file and image position when that data includes them.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Member pages identify sections by backend cuid. The loader turns that cuid into Section Contents so the Section Container can place them. Each backend resource string is both the label and the open target until a richer resource schema exists. Featured image file and position pass through so the Container can place optional imagery. This requirement does not set which cuids pages pass.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Retrieval and Contents construction are one behavior for the cuid input. Resource name and target both come from the same backend string.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-83
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-23
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-121
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Section From CUID SHALL place those Section Contents through the Section Container when retrieval succeeds, and omit the Section Container when the Unified Backend does not provide the section for that cuid.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Successful loads reuse the Section Container placement shell. Omitting the Container when the section is unavailable avoids presenting empty chrome. Page assembly chooses where the Section From CUID appears.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-83
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-23
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-122
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
The Section From CUID SHALL present the Section Header, Section Featured Image, Section Body, and Section Resources through the Section Container presentation, without independent lexical chrome of its own.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Chrome, type, and colors stay on the Section Container so the cuid loader does not fork a second section look. Resource carousel, featured image presentation, and token choices remain those of the Container.
<<<
