[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-GENERIC-EDITOR
TITLE: Generic Editor

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-EDITOR-SHELL
TITLE: Editor Shell

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-180
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Member Frontend Generic Editor Shell SHALL place an Editor Field Area for projected editable controls, and when the editor is available for modification SHALL place Save and Cancel controls, so a member with the necessary permissions can modify editable contents without programming knowledge.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The Shell is the shared placement surface Wave 7 content editors reuse. Field chrome comes from shared form primitives; the Shell owns layout, actions, and edit session feedback.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Derived for GSSC5-84. Hosts project GSSC5-85 form-field primitives into the Field Area.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-84
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-24
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-181
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Editor Shell SHALL fill the width of its page content area, stack the optional title, contention message when shown, Field Area, and action controls vertically, and keep spacing between those regions.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Full-width vertical stacking keeps the editor readable as the viewport resizes and separates feedback, fields, and actions.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-84
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-24
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-182
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
The Editor Shell SHALL use the white theme token for its background, the gray theme token for its border, the dark-green theme token for its default text, and a sans-serif typeface.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
White background and organization palette tokens keep the editor aligned with Member Frontend chrome.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-84
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-24
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
