[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-183
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Editor Field Area SHALL place the editable controls the host projects into the Generic Editor, including shared form-field primitives when the host supplies them.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Content editors differ in field catalogs; the Field Area is the composition slot so Wave 7 hosts reuse one shell with GSSC5-85 form chrome.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-84
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-24
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-184
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Editor Field Area SHALL fill the width of the Editor Shell and stack projected controls in a vertical column.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A full-width column keeps projected fields ordered and readable inside the shell.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-84
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-24
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-185
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
The Editor Field Area SHALL keep small vertical spacing between projected controls.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Spacing between fields avoids crowding without owning field chrome (field chrome is GSSC5-85).
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
