[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-EDITOR-SAVE
TITLE: Editor Save Control

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-186
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Editor Save Control SHALL request persistence of the editor's editable contents when the editor is available for modification and those contents have unsaved changes, and SHALL remain inactive when there are no unsaved changes.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Save is the member-facing write affordance; the host performs the backend write. Inactive Save prevents empty writes.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-84
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-24
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-187
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Editor Save Control SHALL appear in the Editor Shell action row after the Cancel Control.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Cancel-before-Save keeps destructive discard to the left of commit, matching Member Frontend form action order.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-84
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-24
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-188
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
The Editor Save Control SHALL use the light-green theme token for its background, the dark-green theme token for its border and label, a sans-serif typeface, and the label Save.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Light-green fill matches Member Frontend primary submit chrome.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-84
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-24
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-EDITOR-CANCEL
TITLE: Editor Cancel Control

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-189
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Editor Cancel Control SHALL request discard of unsaved changes when the editor is available for modification, without requesting persistence.
<<<
