[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-EDITOR-CONTENTION
TITLE: Editor Contention Unavailable

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-192
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
When another member already holds modification of the same editable resource, the Generic Editor SHALL show that the resource is unavailable for modification and SHALL omit Save and Cancel controls for that second member.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Exclusive edit needs clear contention feedback so the second member does not believe changes were accepted.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-84
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-24
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-42
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-193
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Editor Contention Unavailable message SHALL appear above the Editor Field Area inside the Editor Shell.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Placing the message above fields makes the blocked state visible before the member interacts with controls.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-84
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-24
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-194
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
The Editor Contention Unavailable message SHALL use the light-red theme token for its background, the dark-red theme token for its border and text, and a sans-serif typeface.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Red alert chrome matches Member Frontend unavailable and invalid feedback.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-84
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-24
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-EDITOR-BEHAVIORS
TITLE: Editor Behaviors

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-195
TITLE: Permission Gate
STATEMENT: >>>
When the host indicates the member lacks permission to modify the resource, the Generic Editor SHALL not offer Save or Cancel and SHALL treat projected fields as not available for modification.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
MHLR-24 limits editing to members with the necessary permissions. The host supplies permission; the Shell enforces the gate.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-84
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-24
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-196
TITLE: Exclusive Resource Edit
STATEMENT: >>>
The Generic Editor SHALL acquire exclusive modification of the resource identified to that editor instance before offering Save and Cancel for that resource.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Exclusive edit of a given page or section prevents lost changes when two members target the same resource.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-84
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-24
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-41
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-197
TITLE: Concurrent Different Resource Edits
STATEMENT: >>>
The Member Frontend SHALL allow Generic Editor instances for different resource identities to offer modification at the same time.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Simultaneous editing of different pages or sections must not serialize across the membership.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-84
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-24
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-40
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-198
TITLE: Contention Block
STATEMENT: >>>
When exclusive modification of a resource is already held, a second Generic Editor for that same resource SHALL not acquire modification and SHALL present the Contention Unavailable state.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Contention block pairs with exclusive edit so the second editor cannot write.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-84
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-24
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-42
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-199
TITLE: Save Persistence
STATEMENT: >>>
When Save succeeds from an available Generic Editor with unsaved changes, the editor SHALL notify the host to persist editable contents and SHALL clear the unsaved-change state.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The Shell does not own domain APIs; notifying the host keeps Wave 7 writers pluggable while clearing dirty state after a requested save.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-84
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-24
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-200
TITLE: Cancel Discard
STATEMENT: >>>
When Cancel is activated on an available Generic Editor, the editor SHALL notify the host to discard unsaved changes and SHALL clear the unsaved-change state without requesting persistence.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Discard without write lets the host restore baseline values.
<<<
